@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-10-15
@reviewed: 2026-10-15

Feature: Key Command
  "CLI handler for mason key ls|add|rm: manage which machines may publish to the default server, as the mason user."

  Provides:
    - cli.newKeyCommand @source("symbol:newKeyCommand")
    - cli.defaultKeyDeps @source("symbol:defaultKeyDeps")

  Consumes:
    - setup.KeyList
    - setup.KeyAdd
    - setup.KeyRemove
    - remote.SSHOptionsFromServer

  Invariants:
    - key commands MUST act on the default server from config and fail suggesting mason setup when there is none
    - key add MUST accept a key line, a .pub file path, or - for stdin
    - key ls MUST mark the key this machine uses when it can be determined
    - key rm MUST pass this machine's public key so it is protected unless --force

  OutOfScope:
    - Key validation and authorized_keys editing (setup.Key*)

  Scenario (happy-path): Authorize a laptop
    Given the 'mason key add' line printed by setup on the new laptop
    When it runs on an authorized machine
    Then the key is added and its comment and fingerprint are printed

  Scenario (negative): No server configured
    Given ~/.mason has no server
    When mason key ls runs
    Then it fails suggesting mason setup <host>
